// The Ninth Chimney (bible 8.2): nobody remembers building it. A Guild agent lives at the top: Ostry, a nightjar,
// posted "for a season" to watch the Holdfast. The chimney is anchored; so is he. He has been here twenty-two
// years and thinks it is his first winter (plant 5.1, the Stillness). Chimneys_3.

title: Chimneys_Ninth_Agent
---
<<if has_flag("emberdown.ninth.agent_met")>>
    Ostry: First winter's the hardest, they say. Nearly spring. Then I'm relieved. #still
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Ostry: Ah. You'll be my relief. Early. I was told a season.
Ostry: First winter's the hardest, they say. Nearly spring. #plant:5.1
-> How long have you been up here?
    Ostry: A season. Since the autumn. The autumn was very long. I keep the log. It says the same thing.
-> Who built this chimney?
    Ostry: The Guild. Well. Somebody surveyed it. Then it was here. I watch the ones who walk.
-> ...
    Ostry: You're not my relief. No. Nobody's cowl is that dusty.
Ostry: If you go down, tell the Observatory: nothing to report. Same as every week.
<<flag emberdown.ninth.agent_met 1>>
===
